I was tired of dying with healers, samuri, etc. so I decided to do another
wizard.  Elar was the first one since I started again, so I'm pretty happy
about that.

Elar had always been one for taking the harder path, he never wanted to do
things the easy way.  He and his cat made it to minetwon, which unfortanetly
had a temple to Ptah, but also appeard to be a place that previous
adventurers had been.  Being a wizard, Elar is forgetful, so he doesn't
remember the name of the ghost he fought.  All he remembers is that it
looked like it had been a monk, a monk who had dropped his BoH before dying.
Elar took it.  He also found a magical whistle, which would make bringing
Morris along with him easier.  Unfortanetly, Morris had wandered off and
died, so Elar headed to sokobon, which had a BoH.... So he went back, did
the end of the mines (it was the crypt) with no trouble.

Nothing all that major, found boots of speed in a level 4 shop (lots of
shops in this game, like levels 4,5,6).  The oracle was another bones file,
this one was of one of my failed tourists, yielding nothing.  Elar reached
the quest, but was only level 12, so he went in search of wraiths and
reflection (no reflection yet).  Found an altar, and with the help of
+oCreateMonster, he got magicbane.  found a couple thronerooms, but no
wishes or silver dragons, so he eventually went back to the quest at lvl 14.
The leader was kind enough to get off the throne before he began the quest,
and the simple act of sitting on it netted him a blessed +3 greased SDSM.
Quest was easy, fireball burnt the dark one in 2 or 3 shots.


Headed on, got crowned on his next prayer, and then got to dlvl 21 and the
bones of an unfortante valkyrie.  Said valkyrie had both foobrands, Mojo,
and hte orb of fate.  The poor girl had choked on a titanthroe (sp?).  Elar,
had he been lazy, would have offered a black unicorn on the relatively
nearby neutral altar, but decided against it.  Hit ludios, and with the help
of the occasional pet (create familliar is cool) he bought tons of
protection, got refunds, rinse, repeat... till his naked AC was -2 (and
going from -1 to -2 was TOUGH).  Hit medusa, and for some reason she wasn't
noticing her gaze was reflected (guess I was invisible) so I beat her to
death.  Castle was no trouble, just blew down the drawbridge, and killed
everything in sight.  Wished for a cronathum, err, coranthum, or, well, hte
special pointy hat, a couple magic markers, wrote +oPolymorph, and then
decided that I should go polyless (oops) and held off on a wish, realizing
that minetown only had 4 candles.  Went into gehennom, which was a snap with
0% fail Magic Mapping and (eventually) 0% fail dig.  hit Vlad's, no wish
from the throne, hit the wizards tower (after marking the VS of course)
found a magic lamp just before doing the wizard.  Got my candles, and killed
the wizard.  Level teleported to the VS, stormed through it, and went out
without any trouble.  A couple times the Wizard of Yendor showed up, but the
battles went like this:

WoY : "So, you thought you could destroy me fool!"
Elar : "Pull my finger"
WoY : [pulls finger.  black beam of death shoots out, killing him instantly]
Elar: "Oh, thanks for the !oFullHealing!"

The mysterious force gave me a lot of trouble on lvl 45, I must have been
there 7 times in a row.  Got out, flew up the stairs every level, studied
some spells, and then hit the planes.  WoY showed up twice on earth, and I
think that was it.  Everything was a cakewalk, till Astral.

Started with an archlich and a master lich right next to me.  Well, my last
wish is... a rubber chicken.  Walked to the right, it was Thoth's altar (I
knew I should have gone neutral....)  Killed fammine a couple times.  Did
the middle, killed pestilence a couple times, but it was Ptah's... So I went
left, death gave me some trouble, since his first move was to quaff !oGL,
and then after I was about out of magical energy (darn AoY) he quaffed a
!oFullHealing, so I tried to get past him.  Found the altar, pestilence
followed me, so he died many more times.  Charged up, and went to go whack
death, who went down fairly easily, now that he had no potions, so I killed
him agian, before running low on energy again and returning, to dispatch
pestilence yet again, and then offer the amulet

I had the drain life spell, I had originally intended to ascend with a pet
pestilence and fammine, but after I was ready to start draining, I realized
I didn't know charm monster.  D'oh!

